    "title": "RockHounds offer fans chance to acquire game-worn charitable and themed jerseys",
    "text": "The Midland RockHounds are offering fans the chance to purchase game-worn jerseys from the previous season.\nThe RockHounds, a Double-A Minor League Baseball affiliate of the Oakland Athletics, announced this opportunity in a Facebook post shared on Tuesday. The post included images of players wearing the jerseys.\n\"If you missed out on getting your game worn jerseys during the season, we’ve got you covered,\" the ballclub said.\nAccording to the RockHounds, special jerseys currently available for sale include the Hill Country set, which players wore during a late-season series against the Frisco RoughRiders as a tribute to victims of last summer's Central Texas floods. Also available are blue autism awareness uniforms worn to benefit Bynum School and Star Wars-themed jerseys. A link for purchase is provided in their post.\nThe RockHounds concluded their 2025 season with an overall record of 66-72 and participated in the Texas League Championship Series. They released their 2026 schedule in early October.",
